This tool is an independent re-implementation, for Remotion, of the ideas of
`hyperframes check` / `hyperframes layout` from HeyGen HyperFrames.

Portions of the logic and thresholds were ported (read from the published source and rewritten, not copied
verbatim as a library) from:

  HyperFrames (https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes)
  Copyright (c) HeyGen
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

Specifically derived from the following HyperFrames components:
  - layout-audit.browser.js   (text overflow / clipped text / container overflow / content overlap /
                               text occlusion by elementsFromPoint grid / invisible text / escaped container /
                               canvas edge checks, 2 px tolerance, persistence tiering of findings)
  - contrast-audit.browser.js (WCAG AA 4.5:1 / 3:1 for large text, background sampling with the glyph colour hidden,
                               stroke handling, large-text definition 24 px or 19 px bold)
  - craftAudit.ts             (line_unread floors: 0.4 s for 1-2 words, otherwise 0.75 * (0.5 s + 0.3 s/word),
                               final line >= 2 s; text_below_floor = 2.6% of the short side held >= 0.5 s;
                               dead_stretch > 3 s with the last 3 s excluded; film_silent > 15 s;
                               first_frame_empty; bisection refinement of on-screen windows)
  - contrast-bg.ts            (relative luminance, contrast ratio, suggested compliant foreground colour)

Changes made: the DOM probes were rewritten for the Remotion DOM (root #remotion-canvas, no data-* timeline
attributes), frame seeking uses Remotion's own renderer internals (makePage / seekToFrame), additional checks
(font fallback via CSS.getPlatformFontsForNode, Reels safe zones, ghost text, subtitle-stream heuristic,
ffmpeg-based video checks) were added, and all report text is in Russian.

